{
 "duration": 857.808,
 "timeline": [
  {
   "shot": 0,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Your girlfriend has a sister.",
     "start": 0.225,
     "end": 1.803
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 1,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've met her a hundred times.",
     "start": 2.56,
     "end": 3.821
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 2,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've driven her to the mall.",
     "start": 4.498,
     "end": 5.569
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 3,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've sat next to her at birthday dinners.",
     "start": 6.026,
     "end": 7.747
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 4,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've heard her laugh through the bathroom door.",
     "start": 8.431,
     "end": 12.212
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 5,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Her name is Lily.",
     "start": 13.406,
     "end": 13.949
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 6,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "And tonight, your girlfriend's mother is going to look you in the eye and tell you she only ever had one daughter.",
     "start": 14.315,
     "end": 19.749
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 7,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "It starts on Thanksgiving.",
     "start": 20.832,
     "end": 21.755
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 8,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've been dating Emma for two years.",
     "start": 22.773,
     "end": 24.332
    },
    {
     "text": "You met in college, in Columbus, Ohio, in a statistics class neither of you wanted to take.",
     "start": 24.949,
     "end": 29.497
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 9,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She sat in the back.",
     "start": 30.336,
     "end": 31.218
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 10,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She drew little spirals in the margins of her notebook.",
     "start": 32.012,
     "end": 34.057
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 11,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She was funny in a quiet way that made you feel like you were the only one who got the joke.",
     "start": 34.815,
     "end": 39.005
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 12,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "And from the very first week, Lily was there.",
     "start": 39.985,
     "end": 42.343
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 13,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Lily is Emma's little sister.",
     "start": 43.224,
     "end": 44.588
    },
    {
     "text": "Nineteen.",
     "start": 45.321,
     "end": 45.842
    },
    {
     "text": "Pale.",
     "start": 46.432,
     "end": 46.768
    },
    {
     "text": "Long dark hair that always looks slightly wet.",
     "start": 47.082,
     "end": 49.286
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 14,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She shows up at Emma's apartment without knocking.",
     "start": 50.082,
     "end": 52.117
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 15,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She sits on the arm of the couch while you watch movies.",
     "start": 52.785,
     "end": 54.886
    },
    {
     "text": "She doesn't talk much.",
     "start": 55.626,
     "end": 56.482
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 16,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "When she does, it's usually to Emma, in a low voice you can never quite hear.",
     "start": 57.179,
     "end": 61.151
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 17,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You thought it was cute at first.",
     "start": 62.273,
     "end": 63.718
    },
    {
     "text": "Sisters.",
     "start": 64.47,
     "end": 64.936
    },
    {
     "text": "Close.",
     "start": 65.515,
     "end": 65.869
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 18,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "There were things you didn't think about.",
     "start": 66.857,
     "end": 68.821
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 19,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Like how Lily never eats.",
     "start": 69.79,
     "end": 71.08
    },
    {
     "text": "Not pizza.",
     "start": 71.791,
     "end": 72.512
    },
    {
     "text": "Not popcorn.",
     "start": 72.794,
     "end": 73.541
    },
    {
     "text": "Not birthday cake.",
     "start": 73.541,
     "end": 74.552
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 20,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She just holds the plate in her lap until someone takes it away.",
     "start": 75.41,
     "end": 78.169
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 21,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Like how she's never in any pictures.",
     "start": 79.314,
     "end": 80.727
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 22,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Every photo, every party, every vacation, Lily is the one holding the camera.",
     "start": 81.412,
     "end": 86.403
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 23,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"I hate how I look,\" she says.",
     "start": 87.306,
     "end": 88.798
    },
    {
     "text": "And you believe her.",
     "start": 89.387,
     "end": 89.929
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 24,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Like how Emma never, ever says her name.",
     "start": 90.859,
     "end": 92.595
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 25,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Two years.",
     "start": 92.883,
     "end": 93.909
    },
    {
     "text": "You've never heard Emma say the word \"Lily\" once.",
     "start": 94.819,
     "end": 98.009
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 26,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You didn't notice.",
     "start": 98.247,
     "end": 100.446
    },
    {
     "text": "Why would you?",
     "start": 101.338,
     "end": 101.733
    },
    {
     "text": "You notice now.",
     "start": 103.002,
     "end": 103.613
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 27,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma's parents live in a white farmhouse two hours south of the city.",
     "start": 104.538,
     "end": 108.115
    },
    {
     "text": "Corn fields on three sides.",
     "start": 108.782,
     "end": 110.154
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 28,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "A lake out back, flat and gray in November.",
     "start": 110.827,
     "end": 113.468
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 29,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The driveway is gravel, and it crunches under your tires like teeth.",
     "start": 114.417,
     "end": 117.37
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 30,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma's mom, Diane, hugs you at the door.",
     "start": 118.376,
     "end": 120.833
    },
    {
     "text": "She smells like cinnamon and dish soap.",
     "start": 121.635,
     "end": 123.283
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 31,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma's dad, Frank, shakes your hand without looking at you, then goes back to the football game.",
     "start": 124.079,
     "end": 128.387
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 32,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Lily is already there.",
     "start": 129.555,
     "end": 130.623
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 33,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She's sitting at the end of the dining table, hands folded, watching you come in.",
     "start": 131.24,
     "end": 136.201
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 34,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You don't remember her riding with you.",
     "start": 137.432,
     "end": 138.928
    },
    {
     "text": "You don't remember her getting out of the car.",
     "start": 139.789,
     "end": 141.503
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 35,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "But she's there.",
     "start": 142.742,
     "end": 143.367
    },
    {
     "text": "She smiles at you.",
     "start": 144.502,
     "end": 145.354
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 36,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You smile back.",
     "start": 146.53,
     "end": 147.235
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 37,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Dinner is normal.",
     "start": 148.595,
     "end": 149.568
    },
    {
     "text": "Turkey.",
     "start": 150.397,
     "end": 150.951
    },
    {
     "text": "Green bean casserole.",
     "start": 151.384,
     "end": 152.432
    },
    {
     "text": "Diane asks about your job.",
     "start": 153.374,
     "end": 154.875
    },
    {
     "text": "Frank asks about the Buckeyes.",
     "start": 155.752,
     "end": 157.196
    },
    {
     "text": "Emma squeezes your hand under the table.",
     "start": 158.273,
     "end": 159.978
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 38,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Diane sets out four plates.",
     "start": 161.077,
     "end": 163.042
    },
    {
     "text": "Four.",
     "start": 164.115,
     "end": 164.555
    },
    {
     "text": "Not five.",
     "start": 165.38,
     "end": 166.021
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 39,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Lily doesn't seem to mind.",
     "start": 167.292,
     "end": 168.359
    },
    {
     "text": "She just sits at the end of the table with nothing in front of her, watching everyone eat.",
     "start": 169.11,
     "end": 173.149
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 40,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Nobody passes her anything.",
     "start": 174.258,
     "end": 175.667
    },
    {
     "text": "Nobody looks at her.",
     "start": 176.431,
     "end": 177.248
    },
    {
     "text": "Not once.",
     "start": 177.915,
     "end": 178.471
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 41,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You tell yourself it's a family thing.",
     "start": 179.676,
     "end": 181.307
    },
    {
     "text": "Some old argument you don't know about.",
     "start": 181.992,
     "end": 183.873
    },
    {
     "text": "It's not your business.",
     "start": 184.683,
     "end": 185.494
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 42,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "After dinner, Diane pulls out the photo albums.",
     "start": 186.589,
     "end": 189.281
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 43,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Of course she does.",
     "start": 189.921,
     "end": 190.642
    },
    {
     "text": "It's the boyfriend's first Thanksgiving.",
     "start": 191.003,
     "end": 192.923
    },
    {
     "text": "She sits you down on the couch and opens a thick leather book across your knees.",
     "start": 193.985,
     "end": 197.975
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 44,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"This is Emma's first birthday,\" she says.",
     "start": 198.92,
     "end": 201.472
    },
    {
     "text": "Baby Emma, cake all over her face.",
     "start": 202.338,
     "end": 204.867
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 45,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"This is Emma at Disney World.\"",
     "start": 205.845,
     "end": 207.189
    },
    {
     "text": "Seven years old.",
     "start": 207.996,
     "end": 208.787
    },
    {
     "text": "Mickey ears.",
     "start": 209.188,
     "end": 209.799
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 46,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Emma's first day of kindergarten.\"",
     "start": 210.879,
     "end": 212.504
    },
    {
     "text": "\"Emma on the swing set Frank built.\"",
     "start": 213.555,
     "end": 215.009
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 47,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma.",
     "start": 216.044,
     "end": 216.374
    },
    {
     "text": "Emma.",
     "start": 217.219,
     "end": 217.53
    },
    {
     "text": "Emma.",
     "start": 218.327,
     "end": 218.572
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 48,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You flip the pages.",
     "start": 219.586,
     "end": 220.437
    },
    {
     "text": "Ten years of photos.",
     "start": 221.209,
     "end": 222.573
    },
    {
     "text": "Fifteen.",
     "start": 223.169,
     "end": 223.755
    },
    {
     "text": "Christmas mornings.",
     "start": 224.497,
     "end": 225.365
    },
    {
     "text": "School plays.",
     "start": 225.638,
     "end": 226.338
    },
    {
     "text": "Soccer games.",
     "start": 226.807,
     "end": 227.514
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 49,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "There's only one little girl.",
     "start": 228.588,
     "end": 230.113
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 50,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You laugh a little.",
     "start": 231.378,
     "end": 232.245
    },
    {
     "text": "\"Where's Lily?\" you ask.",
     "start": 233.213,
     "end": 234.376
    },
    {
     "text": "\"Is she in a different album?\"",
     "start": 235.035,
     "end": 236.107
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 51,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The room goes quiet.",
     "start": 237.103,
     "end": 238.19
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 52,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Not normal quiet.",
     "start": 238.99,
     "end": 239.933
    },
    {
     "text": "The kind of quiet where you can hear the refrigerator humming in the next room.",
     "start": 240.573,
     "end": 243.544
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 53,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Diane's smile doesn't move.",
     "start": 244.542,
     "end": 246.139
    },
    {
     "text": "It stays exactly where it is, like it's been glued there.",
     "start": 246.828,
     "end": 249.685
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 54,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Who, sweetheart?\"",
     "start": 250.977,
     "end": 251.802
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 55,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Lily,\" you say.",
     "start": 252.889,
     "end": 253.755
    },
    {
     "text": "You point across the room.",
     "start": 254.1,
     "end": 255.147
    },
    {
     "text": "\"Your other daughter.\"",
     "start": 255.52,
     "end": 256.255
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 56,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Lily is standing in the kitchen doorway.",
     "start": 257.362,
     "end": 259.066
    },
    {
     "text": "Watching.",
     "start": 259.697,
     "end": 260.077
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 57,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Diane doesn't turn around.",
     "start": 261.21,
     "end": 262.374
    },
    {
     "text": "She doesn't even look.",
     "start": 263.075,
     "end": 263.927
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 58,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"We only have Emma,\" she says softly.",
     "start": 265.027,
     "end": 267.219
    },
    {
     "text": "\"We've only ever had Emma.\"",
     "start": 268.073,
     "end": 269.275
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 59,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In the other room, Frank turns the TV up.",
     "start": 270.453,
     "end": 272.656
    },
    {
     "text": "Louder.",
     "start": 273.284,
     "end": 273.696
    },
    {
     "text": "Then louder again.",
     "start": 274.504,
     "end": 275.248
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 60,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma grabs your wrist.",
     "start": 276.353,
     "end": 277.175
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 61,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "She pulls you out the back door, onto the porch.",
     "start": 277.987,
     "end": 279.963
    },
    {
     "text": "It's freezing.",
     "start": 280.581,
     "end": 281.281
    },
    {
     "text": "Your breath comes out white.",
     "start": 281.99,
     "end": 283.12
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 62,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The lake is black now, and something about it makes you not want to look too long.",
     "start": 283.76,
     "end": 288.764
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 63,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Don't do that again,\" Emma whispers.",
     "start": 290.019,
     "end": 292.101
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 64,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Do what?",
     "start": 292.939,
     "end": 293.294
    },
    {
     "text": "Em, what is going on?",
     "start": 294.139,
     "end": 295.308
    },
    {
     "text": "Why is your mom acting like...\"",
     "start": 295.784,
     "end": 297.382
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 65,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Don't ask about her.",
     "start": 298.194,
     "end": 299.206
    },
    {
     "text": "Don't point at her.",
     "start": 299.847,
     "end": 300.83
    },
    {
     "text": "Don't talk about her in front of my parents.",
     "start": 300.83,
     "end": 302.882
    },
    {
     "text": "Please.\"",
     "start": 303.13,
     "end": 303.61
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 66,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"She's your sister.\"",
     "start": 304.452,
     "end": 305.42
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 67,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Emma looks at you.",
     "start": 306.481,
     "end": 307.264
    },
    {
     "text": "Her eyes are wet.",
     "start": 307.859,
     "end": 308.769
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 68,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "\"Just be polite to her,\" she says.",
     "start": 309.717,
     "end": 311.871
    },
    {
     "text": "\"Be polite, and don't say her name.",
     "start": 312.444,
     "end": 314.492
    },
    {
     "text": "And tomorrow we'll go home.",
     "start": 314.92,
     "end": 316.288
    },
    {
     "text": "Okay?\"",
     "start": 316.742,
     "end": 316.968
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 69,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "You've never seen her this scared.",
     "start": 317.992,
     "end": 319.476
    },
    {
     "text": "So you say okay.",
     "start": 320.275,
     "end": 321.089
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 70,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "They put you in the guest room at the end of the upstairs hall.",
     "start": 322.123,
     "end": 324.7
    },
    {
     "text": "Emma sleeps in her old bedroom.",
     "start": 325.25,
     "end": 326.74
    },
    {
     "text": "Diane's rules.",
     "start": 327.432,
     "end": 328.151
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 71,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The house creaks all night.",
     "start": 329.033,
     "end": 330.736
    },
    {
     "text": "Old houses do that.",
     "start": 331.681,
     "end": 332.57
    },
    {
     "text": "You tell yourself old houses do that.",
     "start": 333.557,
     "end": 335.476
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 72,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "At 2:47 AM, you wake up.",
     "start": 336.729,
     "end": 338.074
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "shot": 73,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Someone is standing at the foot of your bed.",
